From b4032f69315572f1fbd42c3cb3084656ddead7fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:07:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] KeyGestureController: Pass Menu and Assist keys on to
 the policy

The hardware key rebinding hotfix returns false for KEYCODE_MENU and
KEYCODE_ASSIST in interceptShortcutsBeforeKeyCapture, so that
PhoneWindowManager handles them. Since 23.2, PhoneWindowManager's
interceptKeyBeforeDispatching is only called at the end of that
function, so the early return skips it and Lineage's press and long
press actions for these keys never run (e.g. long press Menu does not
open recent apps).

Break out of the switch instead, so the keys reach
PhoneWindowManager.interceptKeyBeforeDispatching like the other keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ibdb070cb36f11abcb09e27b37be5676c58799b8b
---
 .../java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java  | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
index e195f1c2f6c0..1f8f66c23840 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
@@ -915,8 +915,9 @@ final class KeyGestureController {
                 break;
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_ASSIST:
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MENU:
-                // Let policy handle it in PhoneWindowManager.interceptKeyBeforeQueueing
-                return false;
+                // Let PhoneWindowManager handle these (press and long press
+                // actions) via interceptKeyBeforeDispatching below.
+                break;
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_VOICE_ASSIST:
                 Slog.wtf(TAG, "KEYCODE_VOICE_ASSIST should be handled in"
                         + " interceptKeyBeforeQueueing");
